.TH HYPER-MATH "1" "October 2026" "GNU Hyper Math 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hyper-math \- Unified C++20 scientific computing & columnar data engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyper-math
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B GNU Hyper Math
(\fBlibhypermath\fR) is a clean-room C++20 library and command-line driver
unifying the functionality of the Python scientific and data-science
ecosystem (\fBNumPy\fR, \fBSciPy\fR, \fBPandas\fR, and \fBPolars\fR) under
the GNU Coding Standards and GNU General Public License v3 or later.
.PP
When invoked with no options or with \fB\-\-demo\fR, \fBhyper-math\fR runs a
comprehensive demonstration across all four architectural pillars:
.IP "1." 4
\fBHyper-Lattice N-D Tensor Engine\fR (\fchyper_math::tensor\fR):
64-byte cache-line aligned \fBslab_buffer<T>\fR, zero-copy affine
\fBlattice_descriptor\fR slicing/transposition/broadcasting, lazily fused
expression templates, Einstein summation (\fBeinsum\fR), \fB.npy\fR binary
I/O, and multi-threaded contractions.
.IP "2." 4
\fBScientific Numerical Continuum\fR (\fchyper_math::scientific\fR):
LU/Cholesky/QR/SVD/Schur/Eigenvalue/Sylvester solvers, Radix-2 & Bluestein
Chirp-Z arbitrary-\fIN\fR FFT/DCT, Gauss-Kronrod G7-K15 adaptive integration,
Dormand-Prince RK4(5) ODE solver, BFGS/L-BFGS-B/Nelder-Mead/Levenberg-Marquardt
& Simplex \fBlinprog\fR optimizers, IIR/FIR digital filters (\fBfiltfilt\fR,
\fBwelch\fR), CSR sparse solvers, \fIk\fR-d trees, and statistical hypothesis
testing / KDE / PCA.
.IP "3." 4
\fBDual-Bitmask Columnar Tabular Engine\fR (\fchyper_math::tabular\fR):
64-bit word-aligned \fBvalidity_bitmap\fR with hardware \fBstd::popcount\fR,
O(1) hash-indexed \fBindex_axis\fR, index-aligned \fBseries\fR arithmetic,
rolling/EWM windows, ISO-8601 \fB.dt\fR accessors, multi-column & \fBasof\fR
joins, pivot/melt/crosstab, and CSV / NDJSON / \fB.hmb\fR binary I/O.
.IP "4." 4
\fBDeclarative Lazy Query Optimizer\fR (\fchyper_math::tabular::lazy_frame\fR):
Expression AST (\fBcol\fR, \fBlit\fR, \fBwhen\fR, \fBover\fR) with constant
folding, filter fusion, predicate pushdown, dead-column elimination, and
projection pushdown.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-demo\fR
Run the interactive multi-pillar scientific and tabular showcase (default).
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-repl\fR
Launch the interactive Read-Eval-Print Loop shell (\fBhyper-math>\fR).
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-csv\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Load a CSV file and display its first 10 rows and \fBdescribe()\fR summary.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-ndjson\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Load an NDJSON file and display its first 10 rows and \fBdescribe()\fR summary.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-eval\fR=\fICMD\fR
Evaluate a scientific or SQL command (\fBroots\fR, \fBhilbert\fR, \fBsvd\fR,
\fBfft\fR, \fBstats\fR, \fBgrad\fR, \fBquad\fR, \fBode\fR, \fBqmc\fR,
\fBsql\fR, \fBconstants\fR).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display help information and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display version and GPLv3+ license notice and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/include/hyper_math/hyper_math.hpp
Master C++20 umbrella header.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/libhypermath.a
Static library archive.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/pkgconfig/hyper-math.pc
\fBpkg-config\fR metadata file.
